From: Press5elect <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 04:32:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] state: the whole-struct size lock is the Android build's
 (the PS5's host types differ)

---
 native/state/def.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/native/state/def.h b/native/state/def.h
index 664819e..e4694b4 100644
--- a/native/state/def.h
+++ b/native/state/def.h
@@ -35,6 +35,12 @@
  * sizes from the assembly instead) */
 #ifdef NC_STATE_PROBE
 #define NC_REC(T, size) const unsigned long nc_probe_size_##T = sizeof(T);
+#elif defined(__PROSPERO__)
+/* The PS5: the recorded sizes are the Android build's, whose host members
+ * (pthread types, pointers to host state, all NC_SKIP) are other sizes here;
+ * the stored members' own checks below still hold, and they are what a
+ * savestate holds. */
+#define NC_REC(T, size)
 #else
 #define NC_REC(T, size)                                                                            \
     _Static_assert(sizeof(T) == (size), #T " changed size: list its new member in its .def (NC_F or " \
